From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: A window being resized is drawn and shown at each step.

Dragging an edge, the loop of the move took the next WM_MOUSEMOVE before
the window's WM_PAINT, which waited until the pointer stopped, and what
was drawn reached dwm.exe only every 50 ms (flush_window_surfaces when
not idle). Explorer, whose layout and drawing take a while, fell behind
the pointer more the further it was dragged. Each step now paints the
window at once and hands it to the compositor, as Windows does with DWM.
---
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
@@ -1125,6 +1125,14 @@
                     NtUserSetWindowPos( hwnd, 0, rect.left, rect.top,
                                         rect.right - rect.left, rect.bottom - rect.top,
                                         hittest == HTCAPTION ? SWP_NOSIZE : 0 );
+                    /* Resized, the window is drawn and shown at once, as with
+                     * DWM: its WM_PAINT would wait until the pointer stops,
+                     * and what it drew reach the screen every 50 ms at most */
+                    if (hittest != HTCAPTION)
+                    {
+                        NtUserRedrawWindow( hwnd, NULL, 0, RDW_UPDATENOW | RDW_ALLCHILDREN );
+                        flush_window_surfaces( TRUE );
+                    }
                 }
             }
         }
